ersonally  saying your weakness nearly undid  everything we fought for  that's who you are he says that the  belters are chanting his name and that  basically philip's nothing without him  he's his heir and someday he will lead  the belt but not until after marco's  gone  and it shows us how marco thinks of  himself how he thinks of this situation  how everything that goes right is  because he planned it so well  and everything that's gone wrong has  happened because  someone else wasn't up to the task that  he gave them  serge comes to naomi in her room and  tells her that  marco wants to see her and we see where  all of this character stuff and all this  setup was heading he tells her that he  has decided to let her leave  but not until after he uses her ship to  lure in the rasanante  and kill her family once she's seen that  he'll put her on the float he says that  philip inspired the idea  and in a really difficult scene we see  her reach out to him  him throwing everything back in her face  insulting her  literally hitting her and just doing his  father's bidding  wanting to be known as the person who  took out the rasanante  marco frames this and everything we saw  happen that was real between naomi and  philip between mother and son as her  trying to betray him he basically  undermines her credibility  and this is the culmination of his  attempt to show  philip who his mother really is as  viewers we know that she was being  sincere and she was trying to help her  son  but we see that he's in so deep here and  that his father's so good at using that  to his advantage  at this point naomi knows that there's  nothing she can do  except walk away and she's left to  follow her own advice  the problem is is that she has to make  it look like she's going to commit  suicide  because if she took a vac suit the  ship's systems will know it's missing  and then they would come looking for her  that's what she was contemplating in the  excerpt i read at the very beginning of  the video  the downside of this is that her son is  gonna think that what he did  caused her to commit suicide so it's a  really impossible situation  and because the ships are separating and  the chet smoke is leaving and this is  her last chance  she makes the difficult decision and she  goes to the airlock  sin realizes this when he looks for her  on the monitors  and he tries to intervene because he  thinks she's trying to kill herself as  well  he inserts himself into the impossible  situation  further complicating things for her and  because this is the last chance she has  he becomes a sacrifice we see that she's  holding some of that hyper-oxygenated  blood  like what we saw them give monica when  they saved her in the shipping container  earlier in the season  we see that she was breathing heavy to  oxygenate her own blood  she exhales as the door opens because if  she hadn't the air inside her lungs  would have expanded with the loss of  pressure  that could have killed her and that's  probably what killed sin  i'm not an expert on these things but i  did look up what happens to a human body  in hard vacuum when i first read the  book and it seems like the authors did  their homework  when she launches herself she would have  something like 15 seconds until she  would lose consciousness  and that's where the hyper-oxygenated  blood comes in i thought it was a great  touch how you notice the red color  around the edges of her vision  as she reaches the limit she jabs  herself with the injector and is able to  make it to the chatsumoka  but while things look pretty peaceful  out there her body is being put through  the ringer she has no protection from  the sun or solar radiation so her skin  would be getting an intense sunburn  without external pressure the water in  her body would be vaporizing  and that causes the noticeable swelling  so it should go without saying that even  though she makes it inside the other  ship  she'll be feeling the effects of this  for some time she's definitely  injured we'll have to wait until next  week to see what happens when she makes  it inside but we do know that the chet's  mocha has been put on autopilot with the  intention of drawing the rasanante to it  alex and bobby could find it and they  would be able to tell holden where it is  but they'll all be falling into the trap  that marco has set for them  and that is where the episode ends so  really just a fantastic episode i was  curious as to how this would play out  because so much of it happens in naomi's  head all the planning  her getting ready her making the  decision that she has to do that  the show did a pretty good job of  setting things up in a way that it made  sense when she's standing there  her interactions with philip marcos  strategically  and manipulatively setting things up so  there's no way that she can get through  to him  she may have been successful in planting  some seeds there but there was no way  that she was going to get him to walk  away from his father  in the current situation so the writing  was good it made it work  and the acting from all of them really  took things up to the next level  it's a tragic situation for everyone  involved and we see how marco uses  everything he can  to shift things to his advantage it's an  episode that was really heavy on  character stuff  i kept wanting to cut things out to make  it shorter when i was writing the recap  but everything was so important  amos had his episode where he really got  deep into where his character is going  seeing him realize that he needs to get  back with his crew  and i'm glad that they took as much care  here with naomi  watching her putting herself through  that physically making the decision to  leave her son behind  knowing that he'll think he's partly  responsible for what happened  all so that she can try to save her  family on the rosanante  it's a defining moment for the character  it was crafted so well  and it was so gripping to watch they  really did pull it off  we didn't get any amos and clarissa or  any drummer at all in this episode  but overall i thought the balancing here  worked better  now that all the stories are kind of  headed in the same direction  just a brief scene with abasarala  talking with alex and bobby but in that  we know that she's finding out more  about what's going on  that she knows the free navies flying  around in martian ships  and even though we only see a little bit  of alex and bobby the scene where she  finds the bullet is fun  and through the communications with  holden we know they're all going to end  up in the same place soon  holden's got himself a temporary crew  and i like the way these characters work  together  they're giving bull some depth monica  seems to be putting together an  idea of what the big picture might be  holden not pulling the trigger  not following through with destroying  the proto-molecule right away  makes you wonder what he was thinking  but it is possible that that was more  about naomi in trying to find her like  he said  and the battle scene was just a lot of  fun to watch so i like where we're at  i'm excited to think about where things  are going and in a few days i'll put up  another video where we'll talk about  that and i think this is a good place to  leave things  because i really want to hear what you  guys think in the comments so let me  know what you're thinking  pretty emotional episode we're getting  some great development of the crew  members on their own  and they're all feeling that separation  and trying to get back together  please like this video if you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already  let me know what you're thinking and  thanks for watching i'll talk to you  soon
 

